o real number \\(d\\) such that \\(x \\star d = x\\) for any real number \\(x\\).\n\nLet's start by using the first condition:\n\\[1 \\star 2 = a(1) + b(2) + c(1)(2) = a + 2b + 2c = 3.\\]\nThis gives us the equation:\n\\[a + 2b + 2c = 3. \\tag{1}\\]\n\nNext, use the second condition:\n\\[2 \\star 3 = a(2) + b(3) + c(2)(3) = 2a + 3b + 6c = 4.\\]\nThis gives us the equation:\n\\[2a + 3b + 6c = 4. \\tag{2}\\]\n\nNow, we use the third condition. For any real number \\(x\\), we have:\n\\[x \\star d = ax + bd + cxd = x.\\]\nThis must hold for all \\(x\\), so we can separate the terms involving \\(x\\) and the constant term:\n\\[ax + cxd = x \\quad \\text{and} \\quad bd = 0.\\]\nSince \\(d\\) is a non-zero real number, it must be that \\(b = 0\\). Substituting \\(b = 0\\) into equations (1) and (2), we get:\n\\[a + 2c = 3 \\tag{3}\\]\n\\[2a + 6c = 4 \\tag{4}\\]\n\nWe can solve these simultaneous equations. First, multiply equation (3) by 2:\n\\[2a + 4c = 6. \\tag{5}\\]\nNow subtract equation (4) from equation (5):\n\\[2a + 4c - (2a + 6c) = 6 - 4\\]\n\\[-2c = 2\\]\n\\[c = -1.\\]\nSubstitute \\(c = -1\\) back into equation (3):\n\\[a + 2(-1) = 3\\]\n\\[a - 2 = 3\\]\n\\[a = 5.\\]\nSo, we have \\(a = 5\\), \\(b = 0\\), and \\(c = -1\\).\n\nNow, we need to find \\(d\\) such that \\(x \\star d = x\\):\n\\[x \\star d = 5x + 0 \\cdot d + (-1)xd = 5x - xd = x.\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[x(5 - d) = x.\\]\nSince this must hold for all \\(x\\), it must be that:\n\\[5 - d = 1\\]\n\\[d = 4.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(d\\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{4}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
